chunk_excerpt:
According to the 2025 edition of the Standards of Care in Diabetes published by the American Diabetes Association (ADA) (25), a diagnosis of type 2 diabetes can be confirmed in individuals presenting with classic symptoms of diabetes (polydipsia, polyuria, polyphagia, and unexplained weight loss) who also meet any one of the following criteria:

- Random venous plasma glucose ≥ 11.1 mmol/L;
- Fasting venous plasma glucose ≥ 7.0 mmol/L;
- 2 h plasma glucose during OGTT ≥ 11.1 mmol/L;
- HbA1c ≥ 6.5%.
- For individuals without typical symptoms, a repeat test on a subsequent day is required to confirm the diagnosis.

